---
title: Getting started
pageSlug: getting-started
mod: spell-codex
section: getting-started
order: 1
---

Install Iron’s Spells ’n Spellbooks, [Spell Actionbar](/mods/spell-actionbar) **1.1.4+**, then Codex. Order matters only in the sense that Codex will not do anything useful without the bar.

Press the Actionbar key (default backtick). You get the Codex, not just a strip of slots. Schools sit along the top. Discovered spells fill the grid. Ink slots hang under the frame.

You do not cast from Iron’s wheel. You do not right-click a scroll in inventory. You do not swing an imbued sword to fire its spell unless you turned that option on. The Codex is the list of what you are allowed to know. The action bar is the only place you fire from.

First useful session:

1. Discover a spell. A Codex page, a leftover Iron’s scroll, or emptying a filled spellbook will do it. As of 1.6.7, that first discover also unlocks **tier I** so you can actually put it on the bar.
2. Open the Codex, click the spell, park it in a slot.
3. Close the menu and cast like Actionbar always worked.

If the HUD is blank, you have nothing equipped yet. That is normal for a new world.
